---
/**
 * The full help text (install, permissions, use, update, remove, retained
 * data) shared by every variant. Headings carry ids so single-page variants
 * can deep-link to them.
 */
import StepList from "./StepList.astro";
import {
  installSteps,
  permissionsTroubleshooting,
  removeSteps,
  retainedData,
  settings,
  updateSteps,
} from "../content/site";
import { links } from "../lib/release";

interface Props {
  /** Heading level for the top-level sections: 2 on a dedicated page, 3 inside a page section. */
  level?: 2 | 3;
}
const { level = 2 } = Astro.props;
const H = level === 2 ? "h2" : "h3";
---

<div class="prose help">
  <H id="install">Install and first launch</H>
  <p>No Terminal, developer tools or certificates are needed. Files with <code>arm64</code> in the name are for Apple silicon Macs.</p>
  <StepList steps={installSteps} />
  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Two separate permissions.</strong> {permissionsTroubleshooting} Apple's own instructions: <a href={links.appleOpenAnyway} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">support.apple.com/102445</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <H id="use">Record</H>
  <p>Left-click the menu bar icon, or press <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>⌥</kbd><kbd>⇧</kbd><kbd>R</kbd> from any app, to record the primary display and system audio. Click or press again to stop. Recordings are saved to Movies → RecordStuff by default; click the saved notification or choose <em>Show last recording</em> from the menu to find the file. Right-click for these settings:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Recording settings" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Options</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {settings.map((row) => (<tr><td>{row.setting}</td><td>{row.options}</td><td>{row.fallback}</td></tr>))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Output is H.264/AAC MP4. Audio requests 256 kbps with voice processing disabled. Actual bitrate depends on the encoder and content.</p>

  <H id="language">Language</H>
  <p>RecordStuff starts in English. Right-click the icon and choose <em>Language → 繁體中文</em> for Traditional Chinese. The choice is saved and can change during a recording without affecting capture settings. Diagnostics stay English; macOS permission dialogs follow the system language.</p>

  <H id="update">Update manually</H>
  <p>Use Check for updates… in the app menu to find a newer version and open its download page. Check for updates on launch is optional, on by default, and runs at most once per 24 hours. Checks wait while recording. Installation stays manual; older builds without this menu can use the download page directly.</p>
  <StepList steps={updateSteps} />

  <H id="remove">Remove</H>
  <StepList steps={removeSteps} />
  <p>Removing the app leaves your data in place. The app never deletes recordings. Delete these yourself only if you no longer need them:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Retained data locations" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {retainedData.map((row) => (<tr><td>{row.data}</td><td><code>{row.location}</code></td></tr>))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>In Finder choose Go → Go to Folder and paste a path to open it. Any remaining entry under Privacy &amp; Security → Screen &amp; System Audio Recording can be removed there; this is optional.</p>
  <p class="dim">The same guide is on GitHub in <a href={links.installGuide} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English</a> and <a href={links.installGuideZh} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Traditional Chinese</a>, pinned to the released commit.</p>
</div>

<style>
  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .table-scroll table {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .help :global(.steps) {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
